  <constraints>
    <constraint source="topology-doc-R1">Container-type owning app is PERMANENT + 1:1 with container-type. Do NOT merge with BFF app-reg. Do NOT reuse existing dev owning app for trial. `170c98e1... = SDAP-PCF-CLIENT` is the ANTI-PATTERN to unwind, not the model.</constraint>
    <constraint source="topology-doc-R3">Standard container-types CANNOT be deleted. Every one created permanently consumes 1 of the 25-cap. Do NOT create container-types "to test" — always via topology-doc-driven owning-app+classification decision.</constraint>
    <constraint source="topology-doc-R5">Container-type CREATE is delegated-only. App-only receives 403. H8 must NOT attempt container-type creation with any token. Container CREATION (`/storage/fileStorage/containers`) is app-only-capable — H8-B rework uses this API.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028-A4">BFF identity is secret-free (Managed Identity + Federated Credentials). Owning apps are E-1 exception (may carry secrets for container-type owner rotation). Do NOT extend Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 in a way that seeds ANY client secret on a BFF identity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-3">Sub-Agent Write Boundary — SKILL.md + handler code + operator scripts are MAIN-SESSION-only if inside .claude/, testable in sub-agent if in src/**. This task modifies BOTH — main-session for SKILL.md; sub-agent OK for handler code (but coordination overhead makes main-session preferable for a coherent commit).</constraint>
    <constraint source="topology-doc-3A-row-4-owner-directive-2026-08-30">Do NOT reuse `spaarke-bff-dev` (= SDAP-BFF-SPE-API `1e40baad-...`) for trial1. Create NEW `Spaarke BFF — Trial 1` app-reg per topology doc §3A row 4 + owner directive Q4.</constraint>
  </constraints>

